						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5974</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5974 is to be kept in a bullet proof glass case in an empty room, which should be monitored at all times. SCP-5974 is to be emptied of all contents and refilled with warm, freshly made black coffee every 24 hours.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5974 is a 24 ounce █████████ coffee cup that has no visible wear on it. Although the size remains constant, the design tends to change according to the current design of the seasonal cup.</p> <p>When the coffee is left unchanged for more than 24 hours, SCP-5974 causes the nearest entity<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-545590-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> to get an urge to find and take SCP-5974.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-545590-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup> This urge will start out quite weak, but increase greatly as time passes. Once the entity gets to SCP-5974 and takes it, SCP-5974 will embed itself into the flesh of the entity, further referred to as SCP-5974-2.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-545590-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >3</a></sup> Once the embedding process has finished, SCP-5974-2 will become enraged and gain large amounts of strength, killing everything it sees until it expires, either by external forces, or exhaustion. Once SCP-5974-2 has expired, it will explode leaving only splatters of blood, and an unscathed SCP-5974 on the floor.</p> <p>SCP-5974 was found on March 20, 1997 in San Diego California. The search for SCP-5974 started after reports of people mysteriously going missing in multiple places between San Diego California, and Phoenix Arizona.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-545590-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Incident&nbsp;Report&nbsp;07:&nbsp;Heaven's&nbsp;Gate</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Title&nbsp;for&nbsp;hiding&nbsp;text</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Details</strong> On March 19, 1997, ██████ Applewhite found SCP-5974 in the woods near his home. He proceeded to pick the cup up and the embedding process began. Moments later, the uncontrollable rampage began, and he proceeded to murder 38 individuals before exhaustion set in, causing his death.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-545590-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. SCP-5974’s effects have only been seen on humans, or humanoid creatures up to this point.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-545590-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. The effect can be reversed by refilling the cup with warm, freshly made black coffee.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-545590-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. This process has been observed to be as short as 10 seconds, and as long as two hours.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-545590-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. Out of the seven currently known incidents relating to SCP-5974, we only have knowledge of what happened on the final one.</div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5973">SCP-5973</a> | SCP-XXXX | <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5975">SCP-5975</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mr-matchbook" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5593151&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607329571" alt="Mr Matchbook" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5593151)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mr-matchbook" >Mr Matchbook</a></span></p> 
